smallworld ABI tables: notices
==============================

The ABI tables in smallworld/platforms/abi/_data are generated when smallworld
is built, and are not part of smallworld's source code. They are derived from,
and modify, data in the following works:

* The Ghidra processor specifications (compiler specification files, .cspec)
  bundled in pypcode, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see
  LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). The generator reads the calling-convention
  prototypes and data organization of these files, renames their registers
  into smallworld's register names, filters and reorders them, and replaces
  some of their values with the values of the published psABIs (the overlay
  in smallworld's tools/abi/overlay lists every such change). These are
  modified derived works within the meaning of section 4(b) of that license.

* angr (BSD 2-Clause License, see LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause-angr.txt) and archinfo
  (BSD 2-Clause License, see LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause-archinfo.txt): calling
  convention and thread-local-storage facts read from their class
  definitions.

